From 27bbe69cb69d5d25d9904e2c076a6d333cbb2473 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RubenGGBC <rgallego007@ikasle.ehu.eus>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:14:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] jakompiled: web runtime: sound through Web Audio

cubeb has no Emscripten backend; the stub made cubeb_init fail and the
989snd player ran silent. web/cubeb_web.cpp implements the part of cubeb
the player uses (one stereo S16 output stream):

- a producer thread calls the data callback (Player::Tick) and writes the
  samples into a ring buffer in wasm memory (at most ~85 ms ahead);
- an AudioWorklet on the page reads the ring through the shared wasm
  memory, with the read/write positions shared through Atomics.

Web Audio only exists on the page's main thread, so the AudioContext is
created there (emscripten_async_run_in_main_runtime_thread). It starts
suspended by the autoplay policy and is resumed on the first key, click
or touch.
---
 web/CMakeLists.txt       |   4 +-
 web/cubeb_web.cpp        | 203 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 web/stubs/cubeb_stub.cpp |  28 ------
 3 files changed, 205 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 web/cubeb_web.cpp
 delete mode 100644 web/stubs/cubeb_stub.cpp

